specs/001-mvp-journey/research.md:38:- **Decision**: Plain `fetch` to `serpapi.com/search.json` (the `serpapi` package uses `https`, which tests cannot mock), engines `google`, `yandex` and `yahoo` queried in parallel (all return organic results as link, title and snippet), the same query for each, one set of calls per research request: `"<normalized name>" <birth year> <death year> (obituary OR grave OR cemetery)`. A maiden name is not added: live runs showed an `OR "<first> <maiden> <last>"` variant buried the real record under unrelated hits. Google uses `num=10`, `gl=us`, `hl=en`. Unknown years are omitted from the query, never sent as `18?8`.
specs/001-mvp-journey/tasks.md:86:- [x] T022 [P] [US2] Implement `class SerpApiProvider implements SearchProvider` in `src/lib/server/search/serpapi.ts` calling `https://serpapi.com/search.json` with plain `fetch` for engines `google`, `yandex`, `yahoo` in parallel (`api_key`; Google adds `num=10`, `gl=us`, `hl=en`). Merge in that order, dedupe by canonical URL. One engine failing is tolerated; all failing → `ProviderError`. The `serpapi` package is not used: it relies on node `https`, which tests cannot mock. Export a module-level `search` instance.
